{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777587-what-endowments-belong-to-extinct-conspiracies-whimsy-thoughtbash","id":777587,"title":"What Endowments Belong To Extinct Conspiracies? [Whimsy!Thoughtbash]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-30T23:42:55-08:00","id":777587,"title":"What Endowments Belong To Extinct Conspiracies? [Whimsy!Thoughtbash]","content":"You know, it would be kind of interesting to come up with some &quot;extinct&quot; Endowments, whose parent Conspiracy was destroyed/co-opted. I can see having scraps of them available mechanically, in terms of &quot;these are the notes you could probably scrape up on how to use the Endowment <i>in game</i>&quot; - you can get an edge if you're just a lone Cell, or can try to expand on those shreds of knowledge in an attempt to give your Compact some &quot;big guns&quot;.<br /> <br /> Here's one that I've been thinking of:<br /> <br /> The <b>&quot;Vierineinz&quot;</b> was an short-lived Prussio-German Conspiracy whose heyday was a few decades after Jung first published his theories of psychodynamics. While few of their own records remain, a patchwork history can be worked out by looking at the records of other European conspiracies who were active in that period. As far as can be gathered, they were avid psychonauts who figured out a method of creating stable &quot;thought-constructs&quot; through (supposedly) mundane means, which they referred to as <b>Daemons</b>. While similar in theory to techniques like memory palaces, a Daemon was <i>far</i> more sophisticated - on the low end, the Conspiracy's members were capable of maintaining multiple trains of thought simultaneously. On the high end...<br /> <br /> Records report that the Vierineinz were capable of near super-human feats of memory, analytic thought, and self-control - while other Conspiracies were better equipped to fight monsters, the Vierineinz were an almost ideal counter to entrenched Supernatural threats. At their height, they possessed a rudimentary empathic network that spanned Europe, could pick out the ripples caused by a conspiracy by glancing through a few different newspapers, and were capable of precisely determining and counteracting nearly any amount of supernatural tampering with their minds, up to and including the mental changes caused by retroactive changes to history.<br /> <br /> Up until roughly a month prior to their dissolution, the Vierineinz were on good terms with the other major players in the European Conspiracy &quot;scene&quot; - it was relatively common to attach a Vierineinz Cell to a given major operation, simply due to the <i>massive</i> increase in brainpower and intelligence analysis.<br /> <br /> It's a shame that they had to be put down like rabid dogs.<br /> <br /> The theory at the time was that a member became a Slasher while connected to the empathic network, thus infecting every other member - though there was some muttering that they all descended into Slasherdom <i>on purpose.</i> In either case, they suddenly declared open war on every other Conspiracy they were aware of - which led to their relatively rapid annihilation, though not before they unleashed several <i>incredibly</i> nasty memetic attacks. Their targets ended up having to deal with unwitting moles for decades after the fact - one of the Vierineinz' more clandestine projects were weaponizing the techniques that allowed them to create their own Daemons. <hr /><br /> In modern nights, anyone who wanted to pull together their old methods would find that anything more advanced than the basic mental optimization methods and &quot;reality checks&quot; were either lost or burnt with <i>extreme</i> prejudice years ago. However, they could at least get the following out of the few remaining training manuals (which were determined to be safe to read):<br /> <br /> \u2022 An excuse to buy dots in practically <i>any</i> Mental merit or a bunch of Specialities in Mental skills - the methods included are almost universally useful in terms of improving memory or mental organization.<br /> \u2022 The ability to buy one-dot <b>Daemons</b> - treat each one as a one-dot Mentor, except A) they are alternate personalities rather than other people, B) can only choose Mental skills, and C) cannot choose Resources in place of a skill. In exchange for being stuck in the budding Vierineinz' head, a Daemon allows them to pass a purely Mental Extended Action related to one of the Daemon's skills to it - if they do so, the Daemon takes over rolling its host's appropriate dice pool. On the downside, the Daemon can't do anything else without interrupting the Extended Action... but on the plus side, the host now no longer needs to pay any attention to the Extended Action, merely receiving the results once it is completed.<br /> \u2022 The ability to buy a specialized version of Unseen Senses; rather than being triggered by a specific type of Supernatural being, it is instead triggered whenever their memories, thoughts, or emotions have been tampered with. It may be focused (gaining the Spooked condition) to immediately indicate where the holes in memory are or reveal which trains of thought aren't theirs.<br /> <br /> Lost techniques include the ability to shunt unwanted mental modifications onto a Daemon, Daemons with <i>much</i> wider uses (such as allowing the choice of Integrity as a &quot;skill&quot;), access to the Advanced versions of Danger Sense, Eidetic Memory, and Library (without needing a massive Safe Place to stick their Library), weaponized Daemons, and their own versions of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/endless-wonder-mysterium-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Egregore</a> and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-beautiful-crime-guardians-of-the-veil-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Masque</a>. Of course, any records of those techniques substantial enough to be used to teach them could be... booby-trapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-01-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T03:45:14-08:00","id":777664,"title":"","content":"If it's mundane (maybe), it's possible someone could develop it independantly from the same basic approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> whose heyday was a few decades after Jung first published his theories of psychodynamics. </div> </div> </div>That seems a bit needlessly obscure. Do you mean the 1940s?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T09:26:11-08:00","id":777790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777587-what-endowments-belong-to-extinct-conspiracies-whimsy-thoughtbash?p=777664#post777664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems a bit needlessly obscure. Do you mean the 1940s?</div> </div> </div> </div>As <i>everyone</i> knows, Jung published his works in 2067. You might want to reality check.<br /> <br /> That was before five centuries were compressed down into one - what, you never stopped to think about <i>why</i> the 20th Century?<br /> <br /> (More seriously, I wrote this after being up for 39-40 hours - the fact that it's in any way <i>coherent</i> is impressive.)<br /> <hr /><br /> But yes, these are methods that could, theoretically, be rediscovered. However, the current trends in psychology... I'd say that it'd be <i>unlikely</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:51:31-08:00","id":777923,"title":"","content":"Giving it a bit more thought; you haven't really given them a target. They seem more like just a group with an endowment rather than Hunters. That's not really a bad thing in my opinion, more an observation.<br /> <br /> I think Beast or maybe Changelings are the obvious targets. Though, I could see them also coming under the scrutiny of Magi who don't like sleepers messing with the Astral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, these are methods that could, theoretically, be rediscovered. However, the current trends in psychology... I'd say that it'd be <i>unlikely</i>. </div> </div> </div>Well, for psychologists maybe. But there are plenty of people who might still take the ideas seriously. I could see a sort of pseudo-psychology group (I'm kinda thinking of scientology there) redeveloping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:36:25-08:00","id":777943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777587-what-endowments-belong-to-extinct-conspiracies-whimsy-thoughtbash?p=777923#post777923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving it a bit more thought; you haven't really given them a target. They seem more like just a group with an endowment rather than Hunters. That's not really a bad thing in my opinion, more an observation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kinda the point - the information given is from a third-party's perspective. If it was from <i>their</i> perspective...<br /> <br /> Their focus wasn't on one kind of monster - they hunted <i>entrenched monsters</i>. Their Endowment gave them the same knowledge advantage that you'd see in a Vampire Elder or an old Cult - or the leaders of most Conspiracies. Also, they had a marked... tendency to study &quot;insane&quot; Supernaturals like Geniuses and Slashers - anyone who got their powers through psychological breakage is a <i>perfect</i> target.<br /> <hr /><br /> Actually, come to think of it, VASCU is kinda using a modern version of the methods, with the leg-up of the Wintergreen Process. Heck, their &quot;empathic network&quot; thing used the same principles as VASCU's Tactical Coordination, rather than anything involving the Astral.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:44:33-08:00","id":778770,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, but if someone told me that story I wouldn't believe it.<br /> <br /> A conspiracy with a social focus with mental powers, if they went Slasher I'd imagine a lot of geniuses and charmers, if not maniacs and psychos.<br /> <br /> So a conspiracy of supergeniuses and people who could sell ice to Eskimos, their back up plans would have back up plans and they could practically mass produce new recruits, those guys would not go gently into the night.<br /> <br /> Tricking the other conspiracies into believing they had been wiped out while they merrily go on their way with sleeper agents in positions they want, far more likely in my opinion. <br /> <br /> Or the going slasher thing is a lie told to cover up why they were really wiped out, perhaps they discovered something that the rest of the hunters couldn't let them know, or risk them revealing. <br /> <br /> And it occurs to me that other than death and going slasher, the other thing that can happen to a hunter is one becoming a monster themselves. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:43:28-08:00","id":778786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777587-what-endowments-belong-to-extinct-conspiracies-whimsy-thoughtbash?p=778770#post778770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Very interesting, but if someone told me that story I wouldn't believe it.<br /> <br /> A conspiracy with a social focus with mental powers, if they went Slasher I'd imagine a lot of geniuses and charmers, if not maniacs and psychos.<br /> <br /> So a conspiracy of supergeniuses and people who could sell ice to Eskimos, their back up plans would have back up plans and they could practically mass produce new recruits, those guys would not go gently into the night.<br /> <br /> Tricking the other conspiracies into believing they had been wiped out while they merrily go on their way with sleeper agents in positions they want, far more likely in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Or the going slasher thing is a lie told to cover up why they were really wiped out, perhaps they discovered something that the rest of the hunters couldn't let them know, or risk them revealing.<br /> <br /> And it occurs to me that other than death and going slasher, the other thing that can happen to a hunter is one becoming a monster themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your suspicions are groundless, silly, and not at all likely.<br /> <br /> You assume that they didn't want to be destroyed. <hr /><br /> More seriously, you are getting the version filtered through heavy layers of propaganda. The other Conspiracies involved aren't entirely sure that they succeeded in wiping out the Vierineinz.<br /> <br /> Their case was... unique. Part of how their Daemon Network worked was that you'd have two people with the &quot;same&quot; Daemon, who would then be able to simulate the other person's emotional responses to a situation (sure, let's go with that). So it would be more accurate to say that one of these &quot;group Daemons&quot; went Slasher.<br /> <br /> And then they <i>reverse engineered it</i>.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, that meant that they could weaponize Slasher-type personality complexes* with <i>acceptable</i> personal risks. They could put on and take off an Undertaking like you would a coat. They could insert a Daemon into your head that would turn you into a psychopathic killer or just dump the Frailty on you for kicks.<br /> <br /> On the other hand...<br /> <br /> *<b>Read:</b> Ripper-tier, not Scourge-tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-03-2015, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T00:55:49-08:00","id":778848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/777587-what-endowments-belong-to-extinct-conspiracies-whimsy-thoughtbash?p=778786#post778786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your suspicions are groundless, silly, and not at all likely.<br /> <br /> You assume that they didn't want to be destroyed. <hr /><br /> More seriously, you are getting the version filtered through heavy layers of propaganda. The other Conspiracies involved aren't entirely sure that they succeeded in wiping out the Vierineinz.<br /> <br /> Their case was... unique. Part of how their Daemon Network worked was that you'd have two people with the &quot;same&quot; Daemon, who would then be able to simulate the other person's emotional responses to a situation (sure, let's go with that). So it would be more accurate to say that one of these &quot;group Daemons&quot; went Slasher.<br /> <br /> And then they <i>reverse engineered it</i>.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, that meant that they could weaponize Slasher-type personality complexes* with <i>acceptable</i> personal risks. They could put on and take off an Undertaking like you would a coat. They could insert a Daemon into your head that would turn you into a psychopathic killer or just dump the Frailty on you for kicks.<br /> <br /> On the other hand...<br /> <br /> *<b>Read:</b> Ripper-tier, not Scourge-tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Based on this, I'm not sure they started the 'war' anymore. I can certainly see the other Conspiracies react to that idea with extreme prejudice as a preemptive strike.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, based on the time period, it would useful and easy to try work how each Conspiracies felt about them before the extinction.<ul><li>Task Force: Valkyrie's pre-cursor organisation</li> <li>MM</li> <li>Lucifuge</li> <li>Cherion's 'pre-cursor</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T14:25:35-08:00","id":783051,"title":"","content":"I leave those to any ST that wants to use them. They're a plot seed, really, rather than a thing with presence and heft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T16:51:36-08:00","id":783128,"title":"","content":"Imagine for a moment that there was an ancient &quot;Conspiracy&quot; way back when the Aryan people first tried to occupy the Scandinavian peninsula. They came and found that it was already occupied...by trolls. We're not talking about Fae trolls, but the trolls of Norse mythology, whom today Null Mysteries call Neanderthals. Well, trolls and humans didn't get along at all. They tried to wipe each other out. The Aryan people were no physical match for the trolls, so they prayed to Wotan to give them an edge. Odin gifted them with the Berserkergang, which allowed them to push their strength and stamina past normal human limits as long as they allowed themselves to be consumed by the bloodwrath. With the bloodwrath of the Berserkers on their side the Aryan people suddenly found themselves on equal footing with the trolls on the battlefield. Eventually, the humans spread throughout the Scandinavian peninsula, and they drove the trolls to extinction. They were successful. Too successful. With no more monsters to hunt they had no more reason to band together, no more reason to be allied and coordinated. The Norsemen soon formed into tribes and turned their violent attentions towards each other with Berserkers as the front line soldiers. Eventually, when their thoughts turned towards other lands they would go a-viking to collect goods from far off lands and bring their Berserkers with them....<br /> <br /> Were they truly Hunters with endowments, or were they early slashers of the Brute variety? Could go either way, or both ways, but if it is the former, then the Berserkergang should be found to pass from parent to child down their blood line. A descendant of the Berserkers need only awaken his bloodwrath. If treated as an Endowment, Berserkergang should ignore all damage penalties and give the Berserker one dot in both Strength and Stamina for every dot he has in the Berserkergang endowment even if it pushes those physicals past 5 dots. The berserker also gains as many points of temporary health as points of Stamina. The effect lasts for the duration of a battle, no matter how long the battle lasts. At the end of a battle the Berserker becomes exhausted, looses the bonus to physicals and suffers from all damage penalties. If the Berserker loss in temporary health points brings him down past zero or if he's been fighting for a whole 12-hours or more in game, then he dies when the ability wears off.<br /> <br /> Modern hunters who learn about Berserkers through scholarly study and manage to track down a modern day descendant of the Berserkers (all appropriate research rolls apply) should meet with the consequences as well as the benefits of trying to exploit a Berserker for the Vigil. When enraged Berserkers can't tell friend from foe, and are likely to relentlessly attack their allies if they get to close. To lethal effect. Also a Berserker who gives in to the bloodwrath should suffer moral degeneration to the point where they quickly become a Slasher after a few battles. An experience like this would make an interesting chronicle for a research-oriented Compact, and serve as an object lesson in tampering with certain sources of power just to gain an edge over monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}